{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016yZDpgBQasFpw3y5zivDPB","type":"tool_result","content":".ard-input/157/issue.md:9:Triage claim logs reason=app-authored for human-filed issues\n.ard-input/157/issue.md:13:Found in the Gate 2 smoke run (#39). A non-lead triage claim on a human-filed issue logs `reason=app-authored`:\n.ard-input/157/issue.md:16:triage.claim issue=61 role=engineer ... reason=app-authored\n.ard-input/157/issue.md:19:`internal/triage/candidates.go:105` builds every candidate with `reason: intake.ReasonAppAuthored`, and the non-lead path that returns a matching stored admission keeps that default. Admission itself is correct; only the logged reason is wrong, which will mislead anyone auditing claims.\n.ard-input/157/issue.md:21:**Fix.** Use a reason that says the issue was admitted earlier (for example a new `intake.ReasonAdmitted`, \"stored admission, body unchanged\"), and keep `app-authored` for App-authored issues only. Add a case to the candidates test.\n.ard/157/logs/triage-lead-20261123T102041.543Z.log:5:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/157/logs/triage-lead-20261123T102041.543Z.log:7:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/157/logs/triage-lead-20261123T102041.543Z.log:11:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/157/logs/triage-lead-20261123T102041.543Z.log:12:[Omitted long matching line]\ninternal/agentjob/admit_test.go:42:\t\t{name: \"app-authored\", is: github.Issue{Number: 3, Author: \"Ard-App[bot]\"}, store: &admissions{err: state.ErrNotFound}, want: true},\ninternal/intake/intake.go:56:\tReasonAppAuthored  Reason = \"app-authored\" // scanner-filed: unaffected by intake\ninternal/intake/intake.go:93:\t\treturn fin(OutcomeAdmit, ReasonAppAuthored)\ninternal/intake/intake_test.go:74:\t\t{\"app-authored without label\", labelMode,\ninternal/intake/intake_test.go:76:\t\t\tOutcomeAdmit, ReasonAppAuthored, \"\", \"\"},\ninternal/intake/intake_test.go:128:\t\t{\"empty Self and Author is not app-authored\", labelMode,\n